# Automated Product Price Tracker with Daily Analytics Dashboard

## Project Overview
An automated product price tracking system built using n8n to collect Amazon product prices, maintain historical price records, identify daily lowest prices, and visualize price trends through an analytics dashboard.

## Technologies Used
- n8n – Workflow automation
- Apify – Amazon product data extraction
- Google Sheets – Product and price history storage
- Looker Studio – Data visualization and analytics

## Workflow Architecture
1. Google Sheets – Stores the product details.
2. n8n – Executes the automated workflow.
3. Apify API – Extracts product price information.
4. Google Sheets – Stores historical price data.
5. Code Node – Processes price records and calculates daily insights.
6. Looker Studio – Displays price trends and daily analytics.

## Key Features
- Automated product price collection.
- Historical price tracking.
- Identification of daily lowest prices.
- Daily analytics and price trend visualization.

## Project Files
- `workflow.json` – Exported n8n workflow.
- `screenshots/` – Workflow and dashboard screenshots.

## Setup Instructions
1. Download the `workflow.json` file.
2. Open your n8n instance.
3. Import the workflow JSON file.
4. Configure your own Apify API token and Google Sheets credentials.
5. Update the required Google Sheets references.
6. Execute the workflow.

## Note
This project requires your own API credentials and Google Sheets configuration. No private credentials are included in this repository.
